{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>If he curse his Elohim.</b> And transgresses the negative commandment אֱלֹהִים לֹא תְקַלֵּל (Exodus 22:27)." "<b>And bear his sin.</b> He shall bear the punishment appropriate to him according to the one cursing and the one cursed in particular — when he did not curse by the Name, or when he reviled. And in this case alone, as in its rendering: דַּיָּינִין לָא תְקַיֵּל (\"judges you shall not curse\")."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:43.251471571Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}